Tcl: let vhpi::get_value return string and real values

wrap_get_value converts logic and enumeration values through vhpiStrVal but has
no case for objects whose natural format already is vhpiStrVal (string generics
and constants) nor for vhpiRealVal, and reports "unhandled value format" for
them. Strings take the existing path; reals become a Tcl double. Against nvc
1.23.0.

--- a/src/tcl/tcl-vhpi.c
+++ b/src/tcl/tcl-vhpi.c
@@ -716,6 +716,7 @@
    case vhpiLogicVecVal:
    case vhpiSmallEnumVal:
    case vhpiEnumVal:
+   case vhpiStrVal:
       {
          vhpiCharT smallbuf[16];
          val.value.str = smallbuf;
@@ -745,6 +746,12 @@
          Tcl_SetObjResult(interp, obj);
          return TCL_OK;
       }
+   case vhpiRealVal:
+      {
+         Tcl_Obj *obj = Tcl_NewDoubleObj(val.value.real);
+         Tcl_SetObjResult(interp, obj);
+         return TCL_OK;
+      }
    default:
       {
          Tcl_Obj *msg = Tcl_ObjPrintf("unhandled value format %d", val.format);
